{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.QuiverMirrorAutomorphismExcluded","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.QuiverMirrorAutomorphismExcluded","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QuiverMirrorAutomorphismExcluded.five_two_forces_count_breaking","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QuiverMirrorAutomorphismExcluded.five_two_forces_count_breaking","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QuiverMirrorAutomorphismExcluded.lean#L96-L106","doc":"**The positive direction**: reading the `(4, 3)` datum *forces* the mirror\nimplementation to change the count — `Ω(σd) ≠ Ω(d)`. Any faithful M1\nconstruction must implement the mirror as a sector-moving action (distinct\nstability rays), never as a DT-preserving symmetry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QuiverMirrorAutomorphismExcluded.count_invariant_excludes_five_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QuiverMirrorAutomorphismExcluded.count_invariant_excludes_five_two","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QuiverMirrorAutomorphismExcluded.lean#L85-L94","doc":"**Corollary at the literature datum**: no count-invariant implementation\nreaches the `5₂` split `(4, 3)` — quiver automorphisms and op-duality are\nexcluded as mirror implementations for M1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QuiverMirrorAutomorphismExcluded.not_chiral_of_count_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QuiverMirrorAutomorphismExcluded.not_chiral_of_count_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QuiverMirrorAutomorphismExcluded.lean#L77-L83","doc":"A count-invariant implementation can never read a genuinely chiral pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QuiverMirrorAutomorphismExcluded.barOdd_zero_of_count_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QuiverMirrorAutomorphismExcluded.barOdd_zero_of_count_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QuiverMirrorAutomorphismExcluded.lean#L68-L75","doc":"**The exclusion**: a count-invariant mirror implementation forces every\nreadable pair amphichiral — the bar-odd part vanishes identically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QuiverMirrorAutomorphismExcluded.sectorPair_swap_of_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QuiverMirrorAutomorphismExcluded.sectorPair_swap_of_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QuiverMirrorAutomorphismExcluded.lean#L59-L66","doc":"For an involutive `σ`, moving the base sector across the mirror swaps the\npair — `sectorPair` is a well-formed chirality split in the sense of\n`ChiralityGradedCount.mirror`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QuiverMirrorAutomorphismExcluded.sectorPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QuiverMirrorAutomorphismExcluded.sectorPair","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QuiverMirrorAutomorphismExcluded.lean#L54-L57","doc":"The chirality pair read off a sector `d` under a mirror implementation\n`σ`: `(Ω d, Ω (σ d))` — \"the count here, the count at the mirror sector\". ","signatureChunk":0}]}